   704	## AFTER MOVEMENT 7 — chapters 45–52, days 111–115 past the Line (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
   705	
   706	### Coordinator rulings (binding)
   707	- **Deployment since the Line: TWENTY-THREE.** Fourteen is Tide on Oryn on the 113th (one sitting, short count then a minute of the long, counted as one). Fifteen to twenty-three are on the 114th: Anchor, looking, at the two stakes (dawn); then at dusk Shadow (once); the read, in the ground; Anchor, looking, for the knot (absent at fourteen feet, faint at twelve, sure at ten); Anchor, the unbinding, palm on the knot (no reach, rate or price assigned); Wind, one burst; Storm, one lane up the old rut; Compression at contact; Ember, one point on the knife. Nothing was used inside the line in sight of the rim; Tide was used on nobody inside any line.
   708	- **Shadow has now been used exactly TWICE and is closed for the rest of the book.** The seal was satisfied on the page: Cael a yard below the floor; Lira on the thirty-fourth step; Seln's back turned; the other three round the door's corner; the rim's six 260 yards off with no line below the hole's lip. Oryn does not know Seln is its source. What the rim has: a fence that failed at a knot set on the edge, and a boy who stood up and DECLARED outside. Teague saw the declaration from the ridge and asked nothing.
   709	- **Tide and Oryn's condition.** At Millrace's bench on the 113th Cael asked leave to set his hand on a BOY'S wrist while Oryn held it, to learn what came to her hand, and was refused ("You asked. That's the rule and you kept it. The answer's no. Next."): the boy's leave was never his to ask from her, and the boy's treatment was not his lesson. On the road, an hour south of the fork, she opened it herself and he asked to read HER; she granted that, a different question, in her own words ("Yes. That's the answer, and I'm the one giving it… the same day as the lean-to and a different question, and… the rule held both times."). [Corrected at close from the Sol recheck: an earlier version of this bullet said she granted the same question.] "Self first" is honoured: he had read himself once (day 102) before reading her by leave. **The debt is still OWED:** two more self-readings on different days, then all of it to her at once; her day is hers; she refused a hurried second ("Not tonight"); nothing is forgiven.
   710	- **The rim:** six, faceless — no seals, names or office; four crossbows and two without, the second Anchor hand one of the six (not the Ostrand-road woman: the same craft, a different weight in the laying). They waited forty paces outside the edge. Their bows are left disabled; their bolts are too stout for Oryn's bow. The crew's five bolts stayed five. The Stair slip's three hundred was taken and never paid. The second paper was lodged sealed with the first.
   711	- **Brom took a bolt** on the 114th (high; missed the lung and the big vessel; "the bolt's the plug"); Oryn drew it and closed it when her hands worked again, outside the line. Exact states are in the author's section below, as corrected after repair.
   712	- **The Stair's chamber:** walls cut floor to roof in five courses, each as tall as a forearm; a line that is not on the Ring stands BETWEEN the courses, on its own, recurring "every ten cords and a piece. Two hundred and twenty yards and a stride" — the Fallow's radius. (There is no continuous groove.) Karis paced the perimeter on the morning of the 115th and got two hundred. The open kit with its contents in taking-out order was found and is carried by Brom; **the case is untouched; the index and the stroke-and-bar are not decoded; nobody theorizes.** "Compact" is not said in this movement.
   713	- **Oryn** was at Millrace on the 113th (her circuit brought her round; EXC-B7-003), crossed for a wounded patient on the 114th and went down under a held rim on the 115th; she is a stop on her route — never "sixth", never "join". **Teague** forfeited a slip to come, held the rim unasked on the 115th ("We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted"); his crew is unnamed; the healer of no Path has not appeared.
   714	- **#50:** Seln's "Six years I've wanted a face" stands verbatim and unglossed; the case's twelve years appears only in his window. **#51:** "Tomorrow makes three" is not explained. **"The still place"** is not said.
   715	- **Length:** the reads split; the coordinator ruled that the Stair's action is not cut for the map's 40,000 line, and repetition is removed instead. **Names:** none minted.
