   115	"The brass was not out. His ring was, by a finger, toward the hill that he drew it from." She did not touch the ring. "I shall draw it where it is when I have had a cord round it."
   116	
   117	The healer had come up last, with the grey mule, and she stood looking down at that water as she looked along a bench.
