   187	It was a hundred and eighty-five yards from the stone to that kerb, as Karis paced it afterward, and nobody else among them could have told iron from a reed at such a distance. Cael did not doubt her. Somebody had come here five cold terms ago with a cord and a mallet, and had driven one stake on the line, where he was sent to drive it. Then he had walked in along that grey path to set another on the lip of the thing itself; and whatever lay under the lip had not cared for the weight of him.
