   197	"It is the old work. It comes up out of the mud as those stones on the Fallow came up out of their floor, with no bed under it and no join, and whatever heaves that mud has not shifted it by a hair. I think that it will carry us." He looked round the five of them. "We shall go as we went down a mile of grass once with a grey thing behind us: at one pace, in file, and nobody stops to look at anything."
   198	
