   128	
   129	"I can't make it," said Lira. She had her right hand over her eyes. "It's not one thing, I think. Or it is, and there's sky in it. I'd be guessing."
   130	
   131	"Then do not," said Karis.
   132	
   133	She was not looking at the middle. She was looking at the ground between, where two faint lines went round the valley's head, high up, a long way above anything else.
