## Densely tracked scene

### Chapter 34, scene 3 (lines 112–176)

Re-enter after Karis's treatment, with her already drinking and testing the swallow while Oryn states only the required voice prognosis. Give Brom's result through a practical action—he tries to fasten the crossbow sleeve or lift the pan—and defer any description of the healed lines. When Oryn turns to Cael, let her inspect and name the visibly half-closed seam before she touches him; Lira's challenge can then force the failed read, after which Oryn leaves the old or Karis-made binding in place rather than repeating the source's wash–bracket–fail–rebind progression. This preserves throat, hand, calf, the protected finding, and the morning arithmetic while replacing all three source-shaped treatment procedures.

No other scene needs wholesale rerouting. Its single finding can be broken locally using the final column above.
